/-! # Source (paper): An Algorithmic Toolbox for Network Calculus
Reference paper for the algorithmic (min,plus) calculus over the **ultimately pseudo-periodic**
function class — the finite class on which `+ / ⊓ / ⊔ / ∗ / ⊘ / closure` become computable. The
Deterministic Network Calculus book's Chapter 4 (Lemmas 4.2–4.6, Theorem 4.3) restates this paper's
Proposition 4. Its catalog files point at the `DeepWiki.NetworkCalculus` library theorems derived
from it. -/

namespace DeepWiki.Bt

/-- DOI of the source paper (Discrete Event Dynamic Systems 18(1):3–49, 2008). -/
def doi : String := "10.1007/s10626-007-0028-x"

/-- Title of the source paper. -/
def title : String := "An Algorithmic Toolbox for Network Calculus"

/-- Authors of the source paper. -/
def authors : List String := ["Anne Bouillard", "Éric Thierry"]

end DeepWiki.Bt
